            <div xml:id="d784">

                <pb facs="1368" n="1354" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg1354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 53D444</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Special Assistant to
                        the Secretary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Battle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-12-01">December 1, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary told me today that in his conversation at the White House yesterday
                    he had mentioned to the President that we were considering possible steps to
                    bring about action in the Far East responsive to the needs of the moment. He
                    said he mentioned for the President’s information only, and not for decision,
                    that we were considering some action which might be taken in Japan along the
                    lines taken in Germany by the Occupying Powers giving greater authority to the
                    Government of Japan. He also said [we?] were considering the cueestion of some
                    declaration which might be made of the United States’ interest in the security
                    of Australia and New Zealand.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ucius</hi>] D. B[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">attle</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
